course: dictionary
lesson: 14781
title: Prudence: thinking ahead
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Prudence means being careful and sensible, and thinking ahead so you avoid risks and mistakes. «She showed prudence by checking the weather before the hike.» She did not just hope for sunshine. She looked ahead and planned.
explain: Prudence is a noun, so it names a quality a person can have. You can act with prudence, or admire someone's prudence. «He spent his pocket money with prudence.» That means he was careful and did not waste it.
explain: Prudence can also mean being careful with money, saving for the future. In Christian teaching it is one of four cardinal virtues, along with justice, courage and self-control, meaning wisely choosing what is right. When it is a girl's name, Prudence is written with a capital letter.
fact: Prudence means being careful and sensible, thinking ahead to avoid risks and mistakes.
fact: «Financial prudence» means being careful with money, not wasting it and saving for the future.
fact: In fables, the prudent ant saves food for winter while the grasshopper plays.
fact: In Christian teaching, prudence is one of the four cardinal virtues: wisely choosing what is right.
fact: Prudence is also a girl's name, so a capital P can mean a person, not a quality.
exercise: «She checked the weather before the hike, showing prudence.» What does prudence mean here? | Forgetting the plan | Being loud and excited about the trip | Being in a hurry | *Being careful and thinking ahead to avoid risks
exercise: In the fable, the prudent ant saves food for winter while the grasshopper plays. What quality is the ant showing? | Anger | *Prudence, by saving for the future | Laziness | Boredom
exercise: Which phrase is about careful spending and saving? | prudence and courage | *financial prudence | prudence and self-control
test: «He spent his pocket money with prudence.» What does this sentence tell us about him? | He lost his money on the way home | He spent all his money at once | *He was careful and did not waste his money | He gave his money away to strangers
test: In Christian teaching, prudence is one of four virtues. What does prudence mean there? | *Wisely choosing what is right | To run as fast as you can | To be the loudest in class | To sleep for longer
exam: Which sentence uses prudence as a girl's name? | *Prudence went to the park with her friend Sam. | She showed prudence by looking at the map first. | Financial prudence means saving money. | The ant acted with prudence all winter.
